  "question": {
    "text": "If $x \\sqrt{1+y}+y \\sqrt{1+x}=0$, then $\\frac{d y}{d x}=$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "tZQwZ",
      "text": "$\\frac{x+1}{x}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "it1kS",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{1+x}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "769Rn",
      "text": "$\\frac{-1}{(1+x)^2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "MnDMk",
      "text": "$\\frac{x}{1+x}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\text {  Given, } x \\sqrt{1+y}+y \\sqrt{1+x}=0 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad x \\sqrt{1+y}=-y \\sqrt{1+x} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad(x \\sqrt{1+y})^2=(-y \\sqrt{1+x})^2\n\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{array}{lr}\n\\Rightarrow & x^2(1+y)=y^2(1+x) \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & x^2-y^2=y^2 x-x^2 y \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & (x-y)(x+y)=x y(y-x) \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & x+y=-x y \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & x+y+x y=0 \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & y=\\frac{-x}{1+x}=-1+\\frac{1}{1+x}\n\\end{array}$\nDifferentiating w.r.t, $x$\n$\\frac{d y}{d x}=-\\frac{1}{(1+x)^2}$",
    "image": null
  },
